# Gargoyle Lord

## Lore

Gargoyle lords are so named because they are the natural leaders of the gargoyle species and possess powers not shared by others of their kind - among them invisibility and metamorphosis into living stone. A lord is considered to be of royal heritage and an elite warrior.

One out of every hundred gargoyles is a lord. One out of every four to eight thousand is recognised as a high lord: effectively a general, or a royal Duke or Baron, usually of high experience level and of great physical strength or ability as a warrior. All lords organise and lead the gargoyles and gurgoyles in war, migration and social structure. Most gargoyles make no great distinction between male and female, and either gender can rule a flock.

The ultimate leader of a flock is the most powerful of its gargoyle lords or mages, elevated to the title of King, Queen, Emperor or Ultimate High Lord. Powerful supernatural creatures - dragons, gods, demons, alien intelligences - can hold that position instead.

## GM Notes

There is one gargoyle lord for approximately every hundred gargoyles. These characters can amass a treasure trove of weapons, armour, artifacts, gems, precious metals and the occasional magic item. An Ultimate High Lord commands an entire flock, which can number into the hundreds of thousands and sometimes millions.

NPC lords range from 1D4+3 levels; high lords are 1D4+5 or higher, and are likely to have a legion of gargoyles and gurgoyles at their beck and call. The Ultimate High Lord is usually 10th level or higher.

Everything else about this creature - habitat, life span, enemies, allies, how Europeans treat it, and its relationship with technology - is the common Gargoyle''s. See that class.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gargoyle-lord');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gargoyle-lord';

